That's not how the math works.  If you have a .32 success rate, then
trying 3 times gives you an overall success rate of (1-((1-.32)^3)) =3D
about 69%, which isn't very reliable.

I personally like my probabilities to be at least 80%, which takes 5
tries.  Assuming you are writing a book that takes an average of 15
charges, that would be about 75 charges to write the book.

More specifically, I would like the probabilities of things I really
don't need to be at least 80%.  For example, if I really needed magic
missile, and I'm not a wizard, then I would prefer to directly wish
for the book.  Well actually, I would prefer to polypile the books
until magic missile showed up.  In fact, my suggestion is to just
collect all the spellbooks you don't need, put them in piles of 4 or
less, make sure none of them are cursed, and just polypile them.



